From 60d041a4755be19286a8fc00985192110ad5e8e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EpicTGuy <20190654+EpicTGuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:53:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Optional user boot hook: start /mnt/Flash/rc.user from
 boot.sh

TimeCapsuleSMB owns /mnt/Flash/rc.local and rewrites it on deploy, so any
user addition there is lost. boot.sh now starts /mnt/Flash/rc.user in the
background when it exists and is executable. TimeCapsuleSMB never installs,
changes or removes rc.user, so additions survive deploy and uninstall.
The hook lives in boot.sh rather than rc.local so that the size-padded
rc.local of the NetBSD 4 flash image is left untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/timecapsulesmb/assets/boot/samba4/boot.sh | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/timecapsulesmb/assets/boot/samba4/boot.sh b/src/timecapsulesmb/assets/boot/samba4/boot.sh
index dfb1d1a5..d6ed0184 100644
--- a/src/timecapsulesmb/assets/boot/samba4/boot.sh
+++ b/src/timecapsulesmb/assets/boot/samba4/boot.sh
@@ -7,6 +7,13 @@ LOCKS_ROOT=/mnt/Locks
 
 [ "$#" -eq 0 ] || { echo 'boot.sh takes no arguments' >&2; exit 2; }
 
+# Optional user hook. TimeCapsuleSMB never installs, changes or removes
+# /mnt/Flash/rc.user, so additions survive deploy, update and uninstall.
+# It runs in the background and cannot delay Samba.
+if [ -x /mnt/Flash/rc.user ]; then
+    /mnt/Flash/rc.user </dev/null >/dev/null 2>&1 &
+fi
+
 # Only one-time platform preparation belongs in shell. These operations must
 # preserve an already running installation: the C manager takes its singleton
 # lock and reconciles old process groups before clearing any Samba lock files.
